# ================ THE THING WORTH SAYING FIRST ==========================================================
# THE CONTESTED NUMBER WAS THE WRONG STATISTIC TO PUBLISH. The l58 red table's last column is a whole-run
# error count, and a whole-run count moves whenever ANY checker in the build changes, whether or not it has
# anything to do with the claim. The claim was about two protocol properties. A reader who reproduces the
# runs on a different base gets different totals and identical per-property figures, and has no way from the
# table to tell which of those two facts the row depended on. The fix is not a better total: it is to publish
# the per-id breakdown, which is what the claim is made of, and to say in the row that the total is
# collateral. Both are below, and the third measurement in Row 1 shows the total moving by one for a reason
# that has nothing to do with the counters.
# DISCLOSURE: I first answered L-6 by measuring the wrong pair, the landing-53 wrapping and saturating runs
# rather than the landing-58 E and F runs, and had to re-derive. The pair is named in every figure here.
